  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with PCA n2000 (config_001) achieves 48.5% accuracy, while image-only ResNet50 (config_010) is very weak at 20.8%, indicating RNA is the dominant signal. The key uncertainty is whether the linear PCA representation is limiting performance or whether a learned nonlinear encoder (scvi_n200) could capture richer structure. This experiment (config_004: RNA-only, single profile, scvi_n200) isolates the encoder effect by changing only the RNA encoder relative to config_001, keeping profile setting and model setting identical. If scvi_n200 significantly outperforms PCA n2000, it justifies prioritizing scvi-based multiprofile and multimodal configs in the remaining budget; if it does not, PCA-based configs remain competitive and we can focus on profile/aggregation or fusion questions. With 7 experiments left, resolving the representation question early maximizes the value of subsequent multiprofile and multimodal tests."
}

